  "description": "A charming period end-of-terrace residence in a highly sought-after city-centre location\nSt. Mary’s, 19 Newcastle Road, is a beautiful period end-of-terrace residence dating back almost 100 years. Ideally positioned in one of Galway City’s most convenient locations, the property enjoys close proximity to University Hospital Galway, University of Galway, a wide selection of primary and secondary schools, and Galway city centre, with its extensive choice of shops, cafés, bars and restaurants. Lower Salthill is also within easy reach.\nExtending to approximately 1,350 sq. ft., this attractive three-bedroom home combines generous proportions and charming period features with excellent potential for modern family living.\nThe property is set back from Newcastle Road, providing a wonderful sense of privacy and seclusion. A welcoming front porch opens into the original tiled entrance hall, retaining much of the character and charm associated with the property’s period.\nAt ground-floor level, there are two bright and spacious reception rooms, both featuring fireplaces, high ceilings and attractive period windows, there is an understairs wc & whb. To the rear is an extended kitchen, which provides access to the property's private rear garden, complete with a garden shed.\nUpstairs, the accommodation comprises three bedrooms and a family bathroom.\nA rear laneway provides convenient access for bins and general household requirements.\nThis is a truly distinctive city property, offering excellent potential for owner-occupiers seeking a character-filled home within easy reach of University Hospital Galway, University of Galway, Galway city centre and Lower Salthill.\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the character, space and location this exceptional property has to offer.",
